⚡🇮🇹In Southern Italy, protests against high fuel prices are intensifying, with farmers and truck drivers mobilized along the roads of Calabria, Puglia, Basilicata, and Sicily. Blockades at the Eni refinery in Taranto, linked to protests by workers of the steel mill, have slowed deliveries, causing shortages at several gas stations and long lines, fueled also by fears of further disruptions.

 At some stations, diesel is exhausted, partly due to a sudden spike in demand. Station operators have reassured motorists that tankers are on the move and are regularly refueling the pumps. Starting tomorrow, a truck stoppage will take effect in Calabria and Sicily, scheduled to last until October 20.

